{"schema_version":"1.9.0","id":"OESA-2026-1572","published":"2026-03-15T11:10:34Z","modified":"2026-08-18T01:19:38.919508585Z","upstream":["CVE-2026-1642"],"summary":"nginx security update","details":"NGINX is a free, open-source, high-performance HTTP server and reverse proxy,  as well as an IMAP/POP3 proxy server.\r\n\r\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\nA vulnerability exists in NGINX OSS and NGINX Plus when configured to proxy to upstream Transport Layer Security (TLS) servers. An attacker with a man-in-the-middle (MITM) position on the upstream server side—along with conditions beyond the attacker&apos;s control—may be able to inject plain text data into the response from an upstream proxied server. The vulnerability is classified as CWE-349: The product, when processing trusted data, accepts any untrusted data that is also included with the trusted data, treating the untrusted data as if it were trusted. This vulnerability primarily affects data integrity.(CVE-2026-1642)","affected":[{"package":{"name":"nginx","ecosystem":"openEuler:20.03-LTS-SP4","purl":"pkg:rpm/openEuler/nginx&distro=openEuler-20.03-LTS-SP4"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"1.21.5-9.oe2003sp4"}]}],"ecosystem_specific":{"aarch64":["nginx-1.21.5-9.oe2003sp4.aarch64.rpm","nginx-debuginfo-1.21.5-9.oe2003sp4.aarch64.rpm","nginx-debugsource-1.21.5-9.oe2003sp4.aarch64.rpm","nginx-mod-devel-1.21.5-9.oe2003sp4.aarch64.rpm","nginx-mod-http-image-filter-1.21.5-9.oe2003sp4.aarch64.rpm","nginx-mod-http-perl-1.21.5-9.oe2003sp4.aarch64.rpm","nginx-mod-http-xslt-filter-1.21.5-9.oe2003sp4.aarch64.rpm","nginx-mod-mail-1.21.5-9.oe2003sp4.aarch64.rpm","nginx-mod-stream-1.21.5-9.oe2003sp4.aarch64.rpm"],"noarch":["nginx-all-modules-1.21.5-9.oe2003sp4.noarch.rpm","nginx-filesystem-1.21.5-9.oe2003sp4.noarch.rpm"],"src":["nginx-1.21.5-9.oe2003sp4.src.rpm"],"x86_64":["nginx-1.21.5-9.oe2003sp4.x86_64.rpm","nginx-debuginfo-1.21.5-9.oe2003sp4.x86_64.rpm","nginx-debugsource-1.21.5-9.oe2003sp4.x86_